I'm going through Baayen (2008) with a gang of students this semester, and 
occasionally we hit upon an anomaly (e.g. actual output not matching what's 
shown in the book - in cases where randomization isn't involved). Since 
Cambridge put the book out in paperback, I assume bazillions of classes all over 
the world are going through the book as well. Is anybody compiling a list of 
errata? I haven't been doing it systematically, since I assumed somebody else 
was, but maybe I should go back and check again (we're about halfway through).

